WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:11.220
The history of gaming extends 5,000 
years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.720
Ancient games foretold the 
futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.200
They were magic ceremonies that 
determined a person's fate.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:23.300
These ceremonies were known 
as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.990
In the present, a young boy 
solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.210
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.300
This boy possesses two hearts - 
one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.210
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.310
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.220
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.970
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.670
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.770
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.140
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:26.070
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:32.320
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:39.590
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:46.330
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.540
Insector Combo

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.330
Yugi, we're here.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.580
That's Duelist Kingdom.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:34.610
Anzu, what if they check 
for Star Chips again?

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:36.800
We're stowaways!

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.210
Don't worry.  They won't check again.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.900
It's more suspicious if you act nervous.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:51.620
Hey!

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:57.160
You should relax.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.420
Thank you, I will.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.650
My heart almost stopped.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.740
You act tough, but you're really a coward.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:14.300
All right!  We all made it ashore-

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.370
I'm sorry, Jonouchi.  It's my fault.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.330
This is how.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.580
What?

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.210
Grandpa gave me those precious cards!

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.620
Damn it!

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.570
Forget about it, Yugi.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:38.220
But I won't forgive that guy for 
throwing your precious cards overboard.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.060
Haga, I will never forgive you!

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:50.980
Attention all duelists, let's 
gather at the castle gate.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.850
That's Pegasus's castle.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.860
All right, let's go!

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.730
Huh?  What?

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.730
What is it, Anzu?

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.930
I saw Bakura over there.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.540
Bakura?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.550
Again?

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.870
Again?

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.140
He's not here.  Am I seeing things?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.730
Let's go.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.140
Uh, okay.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.530
Whoa!  Look who's here!

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:40.170
The Japan champion Insector Haga 
and the runner-up Dinosaur Ryuzaki!

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:43.660
And that's Ryota Kajiki!  
He took third place!

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:47.250
Since Kaiba isn't here, one of 
those three is likely to win.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.930
But I heard that Yugi, the guy 
who beat Kaiba, is here too.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:54.530
If he's strong enough to defeat 
Kaiba, he must be amazing.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:56.580
I wonder what he's like.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.620
Everyone!

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:03.350
Pegasus will now explain the duel rules.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:14.420
Pegasus finally makes his appearance.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.020
You cannot escape me.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:32.820
Let's meet again at the Kingdom if you 
want to reclaim what's most dear to you.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.860
Grandpa!

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:50.380
Pegasus used his dark powers to 
capture my grandfather's soul.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:53.530
You showed up, Yugi boy.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:58.260
Welcome to Duelist Kingdom!

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.280
I will now explain the rules.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:11.330
Duel Monsters cards must 
be used in all duels.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:16.090
You begin with 2000 life points, 
and direct attacks are forbidden.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:22.810
Battle using your strongest card decks.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:29.300
Everyone should have received a 
Dueling Glove and two Star Chips.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:33.970
The wristband has ten holes 
where you can insert Star Chips.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:37.310
Insert your Star Chips into them.

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.860
These Star Chips are proof 
that you are a true duelist.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.730
You will wager these Chips in your duels.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:49.050
I get it.  The loser of a duel 
gives a Star Chip to the winner.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.760
Once you lose all your Chips, 
you can no longer duel.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:57.420
Since Jonouchi and I divided our 
Star Chips, we each have one.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:01.370
The entire island is your 
dueling battleground.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.260
In this battle royal, only duelists who have 
ten Star Chips

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:07.770
will be allowed to enter this gate.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:11.100
The duels will begin in just one hour.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.850
There is a 48-hour time limit.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:17.930
At that time, all duelists with 
less than ten Star Chips will lose

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.790
and be forced off this island.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:25.580
Duelists, good luck!

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:30.130
I promise to enter this castle!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:38.440
Yugi boy, you'll have to fight your way 
through the island duels if you want to battle me.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:42.840
Just wait, Grandpa.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.700
I promise to break Pegasus's shadow power!

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.680
I'm sorry, Yugi.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:53.690
You gave up one of your 
precious Star Chips for me.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:58.650
It's okay.  You have your own 
reasons why you need to win.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:07:59.810
Yugi.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:03.970
Jonouchi, fight hard for your sister.

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.490
We have your back.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.110
You guys.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:12.890
Yugi, we can't afford to lose our first duel.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:13.860
Right.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.820
The duels have begun!

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:27.290
What's your plan, Yugi?

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:31.650
I've already decided to battle Haga first.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.450
That's the spirit!

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.890
Yugi!

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.630
Haga!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.850
Haga, you cheater!  You're running away?

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.140
Yugi!

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:51.740
Wait, Haga!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.730
Keep running!

00:08:56.730 --> 00:09:00.050
This is gross.  How far is he going to run?

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:03.590
Having the entire island be the 
battleground is a crazy idea.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:08.670
I've been wondering why the entire 
island is the battleground too.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:12.940
Why would you need this 
much space for a card game?

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:14.810
Unless...

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:19.910
Did you know that there will be 
new dueling rules at the Kingdom?

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.190
New rules at Duelist Kingdom...

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:26.410
This is what Haga meant.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.620
Haga!

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:35.420
Yugi, I challenge you to a duel here!

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.660
I'll never forgive you!

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:54.640
Haga, I applaud you for willing to battle me.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:58.640
If I beat you first, the rest will be easy.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.620
Bring it on.

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:04.320
Start the duel!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.900
What?

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:10.220
What's this?

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:57.050
This is the Kingdom's battle 
arena - the Duel Ring!

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:57.900
This?

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.910
These things are set up all over the island?

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:03.220
Let's begin.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:12.450
You're already down to one Star Chip.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:16.620
If I take it from you, you're 
out of the tournament.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:20.330
I wager one Star Chip.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:22.360
No, you'll wager two.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:23.530
What?

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:26.370
It's all on the line between us.

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:31.300
Then what will you wager for 
my extra Star Chip, Yugi?

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:34.220
My life as a duelist.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:36.250
I'll wager this card deck.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.750
Ooh, interesting.  Fine.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:45.290
If I knew I was getting your deck, I 
shouldn't have thrown away your Exodia.

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:46.210
Yugi!

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.770
Squash that annoying insect!

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:51.770
Everybody!  There's a 
duel starting over here!

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:55.060
It's the Japan champion Insector 
Haga and...  Who's that?

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:59.160
That's Yugi Muto, the 
duelist who defeated Kaiba.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:04.500
I'm his best friend Jonouchi Katsuya, 
and these are our merry sidekicks.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:08.770
Haga vs Yugi?  It's a 
battle between the elites!

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.700
Here I go, Yugi!

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:17.580
Duel!

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:25.140
I play Killer Needle in attack position.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:34.220
I play Mammoth Graveyard.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.440
Our monsters' attack points are equal.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:42.820
Battle!

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:47.250
Killer Needle counterattacks!

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.490
Killer Needle destroys your Mammoth!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:59.940
They had equal attack points, 
but my monster was destroyed.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:06.170
Yugi, you don't know why I chose 
to battle you in this forest.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.000
Maybe I should tell you.

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:13.890
Pegasus only told me the 
Kingdom's new rules in advance.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.770
Look closely at the field in this Duel Ring.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:21.730
It displays a replica of 
the region surrounding us.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:28.550
Our battlefield is 80% 
forest and 20% wasteland.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:33.450
This forest field is the perfect 
habitat for my insects.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:37.690
Therefore, Insect cards gain 
a Field Power Source Bonus.

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:43.240
Their attack and defense 
points increase by 30%.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:47.170
I see.  The Duel Ring has those 
field effects from the beginning.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:52.680
Yugi, there's no way you can 
win against my Insect cards!

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:55.410
What's so funny, Yugi?

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:59.320
Haga, look at your Insect monster.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:00.540
What?

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:06.140
My Killer Needle!

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:13.000
Oh no!  Yugi's Mammoth Graveyard is perfect 
for the wasteland that makes up 20% of the field.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:16.700
It gained a power bonus 
from the field as well.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:23.380
Haga, I figured out the new rule the moment 
I stood on this platform.  Too bad for you.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:26.710
He figured out the Kingdom's new rules?

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:33.090
I wondered why Pegasus would need an 
island to duel for the longest time.

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:36.930
But when I saw this 
display, I figured it out.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:44.410
The battlefield can give a Field Power Source 
Bonus to a monster card, making it more powerful.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:48.500
So where you choose to battle on 
this island becomes important.

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:56.980
Haga, I only figured it out because 
you led me into this forest.  Thanks.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:02.160
Impressive, Yugi.  You figured it out.

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:05.250
But Field Power isn't the 
only new rule in the Kingdom.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:09.010
There are other rules you know nothing about.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.570
Go, Yugi!

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:13.090
Finish him quick!

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:16.620
I play Hercules Beetle.

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:23.770
The forest's Field Power raises 
its attack points by 30%.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:27.980
The field is 80% forest, 
and the rest is wasteland.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:31.610
But I don't have any cards in my 
hand that are good on this field.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:33.280
I'll go with a combo!

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:36.900
I play Feral Imp in attack position!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:44.940
I add the spell card Horn of the Unicorn, 
giving it 700 more attack points.

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.920
You think you can win with that?

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:55.340
Battle!  Go, Hercules Beetle!

00:15:56.730 --> 00:15:58.700
Feral Imp, Electric Shock!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:06.290
Electric Shock didn't work at all!

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:07.370
What's going on?

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:12.120
Do monsters with a Field Power Bonus 
gain magic resistance as well?

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:18.090
Exactly!  Spells that power up monsters are 
meaningless against monsters with magic resitance.

00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:21.130
They can only use their innate abilities.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:28.270
Hercules Beetle has 1950 attack points, but 
Feral Imp's original attack points are only 1300.

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:31.780
That difference will be deducted 
from your life points.

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:39.010
Insect cards have low attack points, but the 
Field Power Bonus makes them pretty powerful.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:42.010
This place is perfect for that bug!

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:43.680
Hang in there, Yugi!

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.690
Yugi, it's your turn.

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:51.090
I don't have a card in my hand 
that can beat his Hercules Beetle.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:53.810
I'll play a monster in defense 
position and end my turn.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:58.330
If you're already on the 
run, my victory is assured.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:02.320
Beating Kaiba must have been a fluke.

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:04.450
Here comes my special combo!

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:07.100
I play Basic Insect!

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:13.230
The Field Power Source Bonus powers it up.

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:15.920
I equip it with Laser Cannon Armor.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:20.690
And Lev. 2 Power Boost 
triples my weapon's power.

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.420
These weapons power it up by four!

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:27.630
Haga used this combo attack 
to win the Japan tournament!

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.420
Attack!

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:40.010
So you had a Griffore.

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:43.330
You're no match for me from the start.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.650
I place this in defense position!

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:47.700
My cards, hang on and survive!

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.610
It's probably another weak card.

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:54.790
You don't have any cards that can 
stand up to my Insect combo attack.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:58.520
But simply defeating your 
weaklings isn't fun.

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:02.230
I'll set this mystery card on the field.

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:04.290
Jonouchi, what's that card?

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:06.260
Is it a trap card?

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:15.180
When Yugi declares his attack, this trap 
card Parasite Worm will destroy all his monsters.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.210
He's preventing me from attacking.

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:21.410
I can only set a card and try to survive.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:24.650
It looks like you set a 
spell card in desperation.

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:29.740
Watch, Yugi.  I'll fill the 
field with my Insect army!

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.700
There's more!

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:42.730
You're not going to attack?

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:45.600
Or else, I'll keep getting 
more monsters every turn.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:49.110
It's no good.  I don't have 
any monster cards in my hand.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:52.370
If he doesn't do something, he'll 
have to face more and more enemies!

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:55.700
Yeah, but Yugi is prevented from attacking!

00:18:56.930 --> 00:19:00.090
Today is your last day as a duelist.

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:03.890
I'll commemorate it with 
a giant insect parade.

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:06.090
My cards, I'm counting on you.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:07.920
Dark Magician.

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:12.800
This is one of my trump 
cards, but I can't attack.

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:14.490
I play a card in defense position.

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:19.330
No matter what card you play, it's 
powerless against my Insect army.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:22.330
Go, Basic Insect Laser Cannon!

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.940
Your target is that card!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.300
Attack!

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:31.420
What's so funny?

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:34.650
Haga, you said "attack."

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.020
What?

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:40.330
Did you forget that I also set a card?

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:42.390
Don't tell me it's a trap card!

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:46.250
Oh yes.  Since you declared an attack,

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:50.230
it acted 
as a switch to activate my trap card Mirror Force.

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:52.540
Don't shoot!

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:03.900
My Insect army...

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:07.050
All right!

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:08.170
Yugi!

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:12.790
Yugi saw right through my strategy.

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:17.450
Looks like it was a fluke that 
you became Japan's champion.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:21.630
You misread my cards and fell 
victim to your own plan.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:26.700
To put it simply: Haga, you have no skills.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:35.560
He did it!  He'll easily 
defeat Haga in this duel!

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:38.280
What?  We don't know who'll win yet?

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:39.920
Hey!  It's Mai Kujaku!

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:41.820
She's so arrogant!

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:45.040
Whoa!  The worm turned into a cocoon!

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:50.280
Yugi struggles against the Cocoon of 
Evolution combo, a combo that no one has ever defeated.

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:53.210
If the Cocoon hatches, Yugi will be...

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:56.800
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Perfectly Ultimate Great Moth

00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.930
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:09.790
The flask glistens

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:17.640
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:26.610
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:34.390
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:40.220
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:44.330
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:52.610
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:56.850
Shower of happiness

00:21:57.110 --> 00:22:00.970
You are not alone

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:07.690
You're protected by a 
giant ring of friendship
